      "content": "That's a great start and really hits on the structural side of things. To make this dataset actually useful for the classifier, we need to move from the theoretical descriptions to specific linguistic examples. \n\nSince you've identified the mechanisms, could you provide a few realistic, \"text-only\" examples of how these interactions might look in a Slack message, an email, or a meeting transcript? For instance, if we're looking at that \"assumed competence\" mechanism you mentioned, what would a typical condescending comment or a dismissive email actually *say*? I need the raw dialogue so we can tag the specific phrasing for the training set.",
